  "description": "An input action tree written as JSON, stored in a `.model.json` file. A deliberately narrow view of the JSON model format: it takes only `InputContext`, `InputAction` and `InputBinding`, only nests them in that order, and takes only the properties a file can actually set. Unknown keys are refused, which Rojo itself does not do, because a file points at this schema to have its mistakes caught.",
